<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19374" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gĕlōni</span></b> ,
		ōrum, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Γελωνοί</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a Scythian people</i>, <i>on the
				Borysthenes</i>, <i>in the modern Ukraine</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Mel.
				2, 1, 13</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 12, 26, § 88</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Verg.
				G. 2, 115</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. A. 8, 725</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 2,
				9, 23</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 20, 19</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 4,
			35</span></i>.—In sing.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gĕlō-nus</span></b> ,
			i, m., <i>the Gelonian</i>,
			collect., <i><span class="en">Verg. G. 3,
			461</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Deriv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gĕlōnus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the Geloni</i>, <i>Gelonian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">canes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Grat. Cyneg. 195</span></i>
			.</div>
